  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "The source and archived launch profile agree",
      "items": [
        "The retained public607 T1 and T8 profiles each show nine calls: QKV, fused attention and these seven post-attention kernels. This view expands the boxes from the overview without claiming that each internal operation is a separate launch.",
        "The extra gle_o O-projection/boundary fusion is disabled because GLE_T is empty. The fused gle_pr pooler/router remains enabled through GLE_FRT=True. These two similarly named branches have different selected status."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "What the first boundary publishes",
      "items": [
        "b1 normalizes the O branch, forms the gated residual, normalizes the pre-FFN input and writes both BF16 h and an FP32 router copy hr.",
        "It also saves the next residual carry and the squared-norm contribution of columns 1024..8191. That tail lets the final boundary use a sliced unpooler while retaining the full 8192-feature norm."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Pooler and router have different arithmetic",
      "items": [
        "The pooler uses compressed BF16 weights and tensor-core MMA. The router uses FP32 hr and FP32 router weights with scalar FMA, interleaving four router stages through the same kernel. It is not the older BF16 hi/lo router path.",
        "Routing applies sigmoid(logits / sqrt(32)), adds bias for expert selection, picks eight with deterministic ID tie breaks, then normalizes the selected unbiased sigmoid weights. Nonlocal experts receive local ID -1."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "What differs at T1 and T8",
      "items": [
        "Tile route uses one normalization partition at T1 and four at T8, plus one top8 program per token. Final boundary uses BC=256 with eight warps at T1, BC=1024 with sixteen warps at T8.",
        "All displayed compute stages are editable layer scope. PDL and the larger gle_o fusion are disabled here. No source or GPU job was changed to produce these diagrams."
      ]
    }
  ]
